Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:04.74,Default,,0,0,0,,In our home, every story begins with coffee.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.50,0:00:12.98,Default,,0,0,0,,When my grandmother was young, she roasted coffee over the fire in her village.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.50,0:00:21.50,Default,,0,0,0,,The smell of coffee called all the neighbours. This is abol, the first cup.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.50,0:00:27.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Then her children came. They grew up around the same jebena.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.50,0:00:35.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Tona, the second cup, was a time of laughter and stories.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.50,0:00:42.26,Default,,0,0,0,,One day her children went far away. The house fell silent.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.50,0:00:47.98,Default,,0,0,0,,But she never stopped making coffee.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.50,0:00:55.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Today her grandchildren join her by phone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.50,0:01:03.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Bereka, the third cup, is the cup of blessing.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.50,0:01:11.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Even when we are far away, her cup is always waiting for us.
